Time Series Forecasting Methods

These methods are used to predict future values based on historical data.
=======================

| Algorithm   | Full Form                                                     | Simple Meaning                                 | Real-Time Example                                           | When to Use                                    |
| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| **AR**      | AutoRegression                                                | Predicts future values using past values only. | Predict tomorrow's stock price using previous stock prices. | When data depends strongly on past values.     |
| **MA**      | Moving Average                                                | Predicts using past forecast errors.           | Forecast sales based on previous prediction mistakes.       | When random shocks/errors affect data.         |
| **ARMA**    | AutoRegression Moving Average                                 | Combines AR and MA.                            | Predict stock prices using past prices and past errors.     | Stationary data with both patterns and errors. |
| **ARIMA**   | AutoRegression Integrated Moving Average                      | ARMA + Differencing for non-stationary data.   | Forecast stock prices after making data stationary.         | Most common forecasting model.                 |
| **SARIMA**  | Seasonal ARIMA                                                | ARIMA + Seasonal patterns.                     | Predict monthly ice cream sales.                            | Seasonal data.                                 |
| **SARIMAX** | Seasonal ARIMA with Exogenous Variables                       | SARIMA + external factors.                     | Predict sales using seasonality and advertising spend.      | Seasonal data with external influences.        |
| **VAR**     | Vector AutoRegression                                         | Forecast multiple related variables together.  | Predict stock price and trading volume simultaneously.      | Multiple time series influence each other.     |
| **VARMA**   | Vector AutoRegression Moving Average                          | VAR + MA component.                            | Forecast stock price, volume, and error effects together.   | Multiple stationary variables.                 |
| **VARMAX**  | Vector AutoRegression Moving Average with Exogenous Variables | VARMA + external factors.                      | Forecast stock price using volume and interest rates.       | Multiple variables + external factors.         |

=================

1. AR (Autoregression)
Full Form

Auto Regression (AR)

Idea

Predicts the current value using its own past values (lags).

Example

| Day | Sales |
| --- | ----: |
| 1   |   100 |
| 2   |   120 |
| 3   |   140 |


Predict Day 4 using Days 1, 2, and 3.

======

2. MA (Moving Average)
Full Form

Moving Average (MA)

Idea

Uses past forecast errors to predict future values.

Example

If previous predictions made errors:

| Day | Error |
| --- | ----: |
| 1   |    +5 |
| 2   |    -3 |
| 3   |    +2 |


MA learns from these errors.

✅ Uses past errors

========

3. ARMA
Full Form

Autoregressive Moving Average

Idea

Combines:

AR → Past values
MA → Past errors
Example

Predict today's sales using:

Yesterday's sales
Yesterday's prediction error
Use When

✅ Data is stationary

=========

4. ARIMA
Full Form

Autoregressive Integrated Moving Average

Idea

Combines:

AR = Past values
I = Differencing
MA = Past errors
Use When

Data is non-stationary.

First make it stationary using differencing.

Then apply AR + MA.

Example

House prices:

100,120,150,180

Apply differencing:

20,30,30

Then model using AR and MA.

=========

5. SARIMA
Full Form

Seasonal Autoregressive Integrated Moving Average

Idea

ARIMA + Seasonality

Example

Ice cream sales:

| Month    | Sales |
| -------- | ----: |
| May      |  High |
| June     |  High |
| December |   Low |

Pattern repeats every year.

SARIMA captures these seasonal effects.

6. SARIMAX
Full Form

Seasonal ARIMA with Exogenous Variables

Idea

SARIMA + External Factors

Example

Predict ice cream sales using:

Temperature
Holiday
Festival

| Temp | Sales |
| ---- | ----: |
| 40°C |  High |
| 20°C |   Low |

Temperature is an external (exogenous) variable.

=======



7. VAR
Full Form

Vector Autoregression

Idea

Used when multiple variables influence each other.

Example

| Month | Sales | Advertising |
| ----- | ----: | ----------: |
| Jan   |   100 |          20 |
| Feb   |   120 |          25 |

Sales affect advertising and advertising affects sales.

VAR models all variables together.

8. VARMA
Full Form

Vector Autoregressive Moving Average

Idea

VAR + MA

Uses:

Multiple variables
Past values
Past errors
Example

Variables:

Sales
Profit
Advertising

Uses all three plus prediction errors.

9. VARMAX
Full Form

Vector Autoregressive Moving Average with Exogenous Variables

Idea

VARMA + External Variables

Example

Predict:

Sales
Profit

Using:

Past sales
Past profit
Temperature
Holiday

External variables improve forecasting.

10. SES
Full Form

Simple Exponential Smoothing

Idea

Gives more importance to recent observations.

Example

| Day | Sales |
| --- | ----: |
| 1   |   100 |
| 2   |   105 |
| 3   |   120 |


Recent sales get higher weight.

Use When

✅ No trend
✅ No seasonality

